IMPORT prelude

-- Coroners Act 2003 (SA) -- the dates, in one small module.
--
-- Only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH, DATE_YEAR) are
-- used, not the daydate library; dates are compared by serial number.
--
-- "Month" is a calendar month (Acts Interpretation Act 1915 (SA), borrowed, not deposited). A period of months or years
-- "after" a day is counted by the corresponding-date rule: it ends at the end of the day in the later month that has
-- the same number as the day of the event, or at the end of that month if it has no such day (31 January plus one month
-- ends on 28 or 29 February). A last day on a weekend or public holiday is NOT moved: a holiday calendar is not
-- deposited. See NOTES.md, forks F1 and F2.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website (version of 31 January 2023, fetched 6 November
-- 2026). CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Coroners Act 2003`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`cor date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cor days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cor the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `cor the day` a `is before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a LESS THAN DATE_SERIAL b

-- The number of days in a calendar month (the first of the next month, less the first of this month).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`cor length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The day with number d in month m of year y, or the last day of that month if it is shorter.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`cor corresponding day` d m y MEANS
    IF d AT MOST `cor length of month` m `of` y
    THEN DATE_FROM_DMY d m y
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`cor length of month` m `of` y) m y

-- The last day of a period of n calendar months (n from 1 to 12) after the day of an event.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cor the last day of` n `months after` `the day of the event` MEANS
    `cor corresponding day` (DATE_DAY `the day of the event`) `the target month` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the month count` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the day of the event` PLUS n
        `the target month` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN `the month count` MINUS 12
            ELSE `the month count`
        `the target year` MEANS
            IF `the month count` GREATER THAN 12
            THEN DATE_YEAR `the day of the event` PLUS 1
            ELSE DATE_YEAR `the day of the event`

-- The last day of a period of n years after the day of an event (29 February plus a year ends on 28 February).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`cor the last day of` n `years after` `the day of the event` MEANS
    `cor corresponding day` (DATE_DAY `the day of the event`) (DATE_MONTH `the day of the event`) (DATE_YEAR `the day of the event` PLUS n)
